From pearl-miui-camera-6.6-compat
Subject: [PATCH] Decode JPEG input before applying watermark

The 6.6 watermark saver receives encoded JPEG bytes. Feeding those bytes
to the I420 YUV decoder produces a green image while the watermark itself
still renders. Decode the JPEG with BitmapFactory before handing the image
to the watermark pipeline.

---
 smali/S8/d.smali | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smali/S8/d.smali b/smali/S8/d.smali
index 02b58d3..compat 100644
--- a/smali/S8/d.smali
+++ b/smali/S8/d.smali
@@ -450,6 +450,12 @@
 
     move-result-object v12
 
-    invoke-static {v12, v8, v9}, Lcom/xiaomi/libyuv/YuvUtils;->I420ToBitmap(Landroid/graphics/Bitmap;[BI)I
+    const/4 v11, 0x0
+
+    array-length v13, v8
+
+    invoke-static {v8, v11, v13}, Landroid/graphics/BitmapFactory;->decodeByteArray([BII)Landroid/graphics/Bitmap;
+
+    move-result-object v12
 
     iget-object v5, v0, Lxi/a;->a:Ljava/lang/String;
